# Stack to use

## Backend — Laravel only

All backend work is in the repository root (Laravel 12, PHP 8.2): `app/`,
`routes/`, `config/`, and `database/`. Business logic belongs in `app/Services/`
(`TicketService`, `FormService`, `PamanaEmployeeService`), not in controllers.

Schema changes must be a migration in `database/migrations/` — never edit the
database by hand.

## Frontend — keep the existing stack

React source lives in `resources/js/`, bundled by the root Vite config. Do not
introduce another framework, router, styling system, or data-fetching library.

- React 19 + TypeScript on Vite, as a client-side SPA. Laravel is the JSON API only.
- Routing: TanStack Router, file-based in `resources/js/routes/`
- Server state: TanStack Query (`useQuery` / `useMutation`) via `resources/js/lib/api/client.ts`
- UI: existing shadcn-style components in `resources/js/components/ui/` built on Radix
  primitives; Tailwind CSS v4 for styling; `lucide-react` icons; `sonner` toasts
- Forms: `react-hook-form` + `zod`
- Package manager and runner: Bun

Reuse a component from `resources/js/components/ui/` before adding a dependency. If a new
package is genuinely needed, say so and wait for approval.

## `backend/` is legacy — do not build there

The Node/Express app in `backend/` is retired except for two pieces still wired
into the running system:

- the realtime sidecar (`src/realtime-server.ts`, port 4001)
- the PDF worker (`src/cli/generate-pdf.ts`), invoked by `PdfDocumentService`

Touch these only to fix bugs in those two paths. Never add a new feature or
endpoint here — it goes in Laravel.

Note the schema drift risk: the ticketing users table is `users_`, and `users`
holds login credentials only. Laravel's `User` model already points at `users_`.
